WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.334
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.267
You are making your talk-show
debut, is that correct?

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.300
-Yeah.
-Ah, welcome.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.901
Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:08.434
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:09.667
-Oh, thank you for having me.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:12.968
-I also heard that
you're also filming a movie

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.601
now with our pal
Jennifer Garner...

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.267
-Yeah.
-...who I love her so much.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:17.634
Please give her our --
-Oh, I love her.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.400
-Yeah, she's the best.
-She's incredible.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.067
She's so sweet.
-She plays your mom?

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:23.033
-She does, and she reminds me of
my actual mom,

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.234
so it works out for the best.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:25.601
-Is actual mom here?

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.701
-My actual mom is here.
I don't know -- I can't see --

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.000
-Actual mom, are you here?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Actual mom.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:34.234
Yeah, actual mom!

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.634
Hi, mom!

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.701
-I knew she was going to cry.
I knew it.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.567
-Aww! She's got to be proud.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.968
You got to be proud of
your girl here.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.033
Was your mom excited that
Jennifer Garner is playing her?

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.367
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.300
I think my dad
was more excited, though.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:53.968
-Emma, I wanted to ask you
about this,

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:57.734
because I read this online,
that you're a big fan of a band

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.901
and you like to --
When you're talking to people,

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.567
you like to introduce
this band to people

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.033
if they don't know of this.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.501
-I will introduce
if people ask me to,

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:06.634
but I'm not going to --

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:07.834
-Well, I would like to ask you.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.934
-Okay. Then I'll introduce it
to everybody.

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.868
-Yeah.
What is the name of the band?

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.601
-Seventeen.
-Seventeen.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.901
-Uh-huh.
-Now, you're into this band?

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.367
How long have you been
into Seventeen?

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:20.567
-I was 15,
so about five years ago.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.434
-You're 15 into Seventeen.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:23.567
-Yeah.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.567
-And we have a photo of
Seventeen, okay?

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:29.067
This is Seventeen?
-Yeah, that's them.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.234
-Wow. A lot of people.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.667
-Yeah. Only 13, but...

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:34.834
-There's 13 people in Seventeen.

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:37.167
-13 in Seventeen, yeah.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.567
It's a whole thing.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.133
-So there's 13 people
in Seventeen.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.634
-Okay, I'll explain
the numbers, okay?

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.167
There's 13 of them,
so it's 13, right?

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.734
And there are
three different groups.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.934
You have hip-hop,
performance, and vocal.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.267
And then there's one team.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:55.100
So 13 plus 3 plus 1 is 17.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.534
-Okay. Yeah, alright. I'm in.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:58.634
-Yeah.
-I like that.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.434
-I know. It's a good thing.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:03.100
-Do you have a song I should
download or get on my playlist?

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.834
-Ooh! My favorite song is --

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.534
I think everybody would kind of
like this song called "To You."

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:09.534
-Okay.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.734
-It's really fun. It's upbeat.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:14.300
It's got a great story
behind it, so...

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.901
-I just like
you're so charming selling this.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.801
It is everyone's
favorite song right now.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:19.801
Yeah, we love it.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.000
Everybody listen to it.
-Yeah.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.501
Let's talk about "Wednesday."

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:25.467
It is the second-most-watched
show in the history of Netflix.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.701
People can't get enough of it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.167
Jenna Ortega
was just on our show,

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.801
and she's phenomenal.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:39.167
And you go, "Oh, my gosh,
who is this kid?"

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.901
And then you show up
in this scene, I go, "Wow!

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.400
Who is this kid? Oh, my God.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.167
Look at these talented actors."
I mean, you're phenomenal.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.801
Did you know of
"The Addams Family"

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.033
going into this,
that you were --

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:52.634
-I had watched
the '90s movies growing up,

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:55.033
but I didn't know it was,
like, a TV show

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.167
and there's a
comic and everything.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.734
I had no idea.

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:58.868
So, then, when I got the role,

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.400
I kind of dove into it,
and I love it.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.601
It's so fun.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.467
-And you knew --
You go, "Well --"

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.200
You probably get the script,
and you go,

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.601
"I think I want to play Enid,
I'll play the roommate,"

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:11.334
or do you want to -- Do you go,
"I want to be Wednesday."

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.267
-I'm not a good Wednesday.
-You're not a good Wednesday.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:14.300
-No.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.467
-Could you play Wednesday
at all?

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.167
I mean, do you
have any Wednesday in you

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.434
or are you just positive?

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.834
-I'm -- Wednesday
does not come to me naturally.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.234
Enid does.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:26.033
And I think Jenna did such
a flawless job with Wednesday

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:29.400
that if I even tried,
it would just be a disgrace.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.834
-No! You're so funny.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.701
-It would not be --

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.267
-But are you an optimist?
Are you a...

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:36.701
-Yeah, I'm an optimist.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:39.100
I think that's one of the only
things I have in common with

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.100
Enid is that I am an optimist.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.367
I don't like wearing
colorful clothes.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:46.901
I don't -- I'm not an extrovert.
I'm an introvert.

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.200
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.634
-But what you just said, I'm...

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.667
It's very interesting,

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.734
because I would think
that would be Wednesday.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:55.834
-You'd think, but I just
can't pull it off.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:59.000
-Yeah, I know.
No, I'm a disgrace.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.534
I mean, I really am.
I'm a total disgrace.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.067
But then you get to turn into
a werewolf.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.667
-Uh-huh.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:08.667
Was there werewolf training?
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:11.567
-I'm being serious.
-No, I'm serious, too.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:16.067
-So they go to training --
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:19.467
-Yeah. And you got to --
-Yeah, the whole thing.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.200
We did this
werewolf boot camp one time,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.434
because there's Episode 6,

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.267
where the parents come
and all the family comes.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:29.100
I had four or five brothers,

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.601
and they really had to get
them into the werewolf spirit.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:35.033
So they asked me to come in
and do, you know,

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.300
werewolf boot camp,
and I was like,

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.334
"Okay, what does this mean?"

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:38.434
-Werewolf boot camp.
So, that's --

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:40.200
-Yeah, it's like --

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.400
-Professionally,
people do this for a living?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.367
-They, like --
-Werewolf boot camp.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.734
-I've never done so much
parkour in my life.

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.701
It was me, like...
-I'm assuming.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.701
-...running on the floor
on all fours,

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.167
leaping over things.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:55.501
I had to -- We had these stunt
guys pretending to be sheep,

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:59.000
and we would, like,
crawl around them in a circle.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.901
-Mom, were you there
on set for this?

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:02.133
I just want to make sure
this is legit.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.501
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.334
-It was -- I think anybody
who was walking past was like...

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:06.934
-Stuntmen pretending
to be sheep.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.501
Yeah, I love it.
-..."What is going on in there?"

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.000
-But you nailed it. It worked.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.434
-It worked.
-Yeah, it worked.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:12.701
Yeah, congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:14.367
-I'm so happy you're here on
"The Tonight Show,"

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:15.434
making your debut with us.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:16.634
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.901
Here's Emma Myers in
"Wednesday." Take a look.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.400
-Howdy, roomie.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.634
-Wednesday,
this is Enid Sinclair.

00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:29.834
-Are you feeling okay?
You look a little...pale.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:33.067
-Wednesday always looks
half dead.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:34.834
-Oh.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.334
Welcome to Ophelia Hall.

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:40.133
Not a hugger. Got it.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.667
-Please excuse Wednesday.

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:43.934
She's allergic to color.

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:45.234
-Oh, wow.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:46.634
What happens to you?

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:48.634
-I break out into hives,

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:50.400
and then the flesh
peels off my bones.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.567
-"Oh."

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:57.200
That's Emma Myers right there.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.968
Season 1 of "Wednesday"
is streaming now on Netflix.

